cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the HPEC 2026 paper below. If you need to cite the
  software itself (a specific version, or the framework rather than the study), cite this
  record as well.
title: "abstraction-regret: a framework for measuring what a GPU DSL forecloses, at a fixed algorithm"
abstract: >-
  Research software measuring "abstraction regret" -- the performance a GPU DSL forecloses,
  at a fixed algorithm, because it cannot express the memory layout or the control flow a
  workload needs. Instantiated on finite automata across two faces (control-flow-bound NFA
  simulation, memory-bound DFA simulation) and a paradigm axis (CUDA and NVIDIA Warp on the
  thread-SIMT side, Triton and Gluon on the tile/SPMD side), with a CPU reference oracle that
  every GPU kernel is validated bit-for-bit against and a falsifiable Triton/Gluon control.
type: software
